 "captions": [
  {
   "from": 30,
   "dur": 105,
   "text": "Every time you ask a chatbot a question, something happens that you never see."
  },
  {
   "from": 146,
   "dur": 81,
   "text": "Somewhere, in a building the size of several football pitches,"
  },
  {
   "from": 228,
   "dur": 51,
   "text": "thousands of chips run a little hotter."
  },
  {
   "from": 288,
   "dur": 52,
   "text": "Pumps push coolant through the racks."
  },
  {
   "from": 340,
   "dur": 84,
   "text": "And beyond the fence line, a power grid strains to keep up."
  },
  {
   "from": 439,
   "dur": 96,
   "text": "We talk about artificial intelligence as if it were weightless."
  },
  {
   "from": 535,
   "dur": 40,
   "text": "Software. Code. The cloud."
  },
  {
   "from": 587,
   "dur": 108,
   "text": "But the AI boom runs on concrete, copper, steel and electricity."
  },
  {
   "from": 708,
   "dur": 57,
   "text": "And some of its biggest winners make nothing"
  },
  {
   "from": 765,
   "dur": 57,
   "text": "you would ever call artificial intelligence."
  },
  {
   "from": 998,
   "dur": 65,
   "text": "Follow the money, and it starts with four companies."
  },
  {
   "from": 1073,
   "dur": 107,
   "text": "In their latest financial years, Microsoft, Alphabet, Amazon and Meta"
  },
  {
   "from": 1180,
   "dur": 119,
   "text": "together spent more than four hundred billion dollars on capital expenditure."
  },
  {
   "from": 1308,
   "dur": 93,
   "text": "And they are accelerating. Amazon alone expects to spend"
  },
  {
   "from": 1401,
   "dur": 89,
   "text": "around two hundred and twenty billion dollars in 2026."
  },
  {
   "from": 1500,
   "dur": 116,
   "text": "Most of that money pays for one thing: data centres, filled with AI chips."
  },
  {
   "from": 1646,
   "dur": 84,
   "text": "To see who captures that money, picture AI as a stack."
  },
  {
   "from": 1740,
   "dur": 77,
   "text": "At the top, the applications and models. Below them,"
  },
  {
   "from": 1817,
   "dur": 74,
   "text": "the chips. Then the factories that make the chips."
  },
  {
   "from": 1899,
   "dur": 100,
   "text": "The data centres that house them. The power stations that feed them."
  },
  {
   "from": 1999,
   "dur": 74,
   "text": "The lines and substations that deliver that power."
  },
  {
   "from": 2081,
   "dur": 55,
   "text": "And at the very bottom, the transformers,"
  },
  {
   "from": 2136,
   "dur": 84,
   "text": "switchgear and cables that make all of it physically possible."
  },
  {
   "from": 2233,
   "dur": 103,
   "text": "Most of the attention sits at the top. This story goes all the way down."
  },
  {
   "from": 2386,
   "dur": 51,
   "text": "The most visible winner is Nvidia."
  },
  {
   "from": 2445,
   "dur": 64,
   "text": "In the three months to October 2026,"
  },
  {
   "from": 2509,
   "dur": 124,
   "text": "it reported revenue of almost one hundred and sixteen billion dollars."
  },
  {
   "from": 2641,
   "dur": 80,
   "text": "More than ninety percent of it came from data centres."
  },
  {
   "from": 2721,
   "dur": 106,
   "text": "And it kept roughly seventy-five cents of every dollar as gross profit."
  },
  {
   "from": 2839,
   "dur": 83,
   "text": "But Nvidia does not make its own chips. It designs them."
  },
  {
   "from": 2941,
   "dur": 136,
   "text": "Manufacturing goes to Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company, or TSMC."
  },
  {
   "from": 3085,
   "dur": 101,
   "text": "By one industry estimate, it took nearly three-quarters of all"
  },
  {
   "from": 3187,
   "dur": 95,
   "text": "contract chipmaking revenue in the second quarter of 2026."
  },
  {
   "from": 3289,
   "dur": 107,
   "text": "High-performance computing now makes up about two-thirds of its sales."
  },
  {
   "from": 3396,
   "dur": 75,
   "text": "And it has told investors it plans to spend up to"
  },
  {
   "from": 3470,
   "dur": 81,
   "text": "sixty-four billion dollars on new capacity this year."
  },
  {
   "from": 3564,
   "dur": 85,
   "text": "TSMC, in turn, relies on a single Dutch company."
  },
  {
   "from": 3656,
   "dur": 90,
   "text": "ASML is the world's only maker of the extreme ultraviolet"
  },
  {
   "from": 3746,
   "dur": 93,
   "text": "lithography machines used to print the most advanced chips."
  },
  {
   "from": 3846,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "The newest models are reported to cost hundreds of millions of dollars each."
  },
  {
   "from": 3963,
   "dur": 102,
   "text": "Then there is memory. SK hynix makes the high-bandwidth memory"
  },
  {
   "from": 4065,
   "dur": 92,
   "text": "stacked beside each AI processor. In its latest quarter,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4157,
   "dur": 94,
   "text": "it reported an operating margin of around eighty percent."
  },
  {
   "from": 4261,
   "dur": 122,
   "text": "And the finished pieces must be bonded together, in a process called advanced"
  },
  {
   "from": 4383,
   "dur": 112,
   "text": "packaging. Another bottleneck, and another place TSMC is pouring money."
  },
  {
   "from": 4520,
   "dur": 50,
   "text": "Each link captures value differently."
  },
  {
   "from": 4578,
   "dur": 61,
   "text": "The designer earns the richest margins."
  },
  {
   "from": 4639,
   "dur": 130,
   "text": "The manufacturer carries the heaviest capital bill. The toolmaker holds a monopoly."
  },
  {
   "from": 4778,
   "dur": 65,
   "text": "But all of them depend on the same customers,"
  },
  {
   "from": 4844,
   "dur": 76,
   "text": "and those customers are building something enormous."
  },
  {
   "from": 4962,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "A chip is only useful inside a building that can power it and cool it."
  },
  {
   "from": 5075,
   "dur": 135,
   "text": "And an AI data centre is not a warehouse of computers. It is an industrial machine."
  },
  {
   "from": 5221,
   "dur": 129,
   "text": "Nvidia's latest rack-scale systems are specified at around one hundred and twenty"
  },
  {
   "from": 5350,
   "dur": 126,
   "text": "kilowatts per rack. That's many times what a typical server rack was built for."
  },
  {
   "from": 5484,
   "dur": 60,
   "text": "Air can no longer carry that much heat away."
  },
  {
   "from": 5544,
   "dur": 56,
   "text": "So liquid is piped straight to the chips."
  },
  {
   "from": 5620,
   "dur": 92,
   "text": "That has turned cooling and power equipment into a growth industry."
  },
  {
   "from": 5720,
   "dur": 103,
   "text": "Vertiv, which makes both, reported a sixty-one percent jump in sales"
  },
  {
   "from": 5823,
   "dur": 99,
   "text": "in its latest quarter, and said organic orders more than doubled."
  },
  {
   "from": 5929,
   "dur": 61,
   "text": "Eaton, which makes electrical equipment,"
  },
  {
   "from": 5990,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "says the backlog in its electrical business is up forty-six percent."
  },
  {
   "from": 6106,
   "dur": 120,
   "text": "McKinsey estimates that of the money going into AI data centres this decade,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6226,
   "dur": 74,
   "text": "about sixty percent goes on chips and hardware,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6300,
   "dur": 99,
   "text": "and about a quarter on power, cooling and electrical equipment."
  },
  {
   "from": 6411,
   "dur": 117,
   "text": "And space is still scarce. In North America's main markets,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6528,
   "dur": 132,
   "text": "the property firm CBRE puts vacancy at a record low of 1.4 percent."
  },
  {
   "from": 6668,
   "dur": 85,
   "text": "Some of it is being built on borrowed money. CoreWeave,"
  },
  {
   "from": 6753,
   "dur": 113,
   "text": "which rents out Nvidia chips, reports a contract backlog of more than one"
  },
  {
   "from": 6865,
   "dur": 116,
   "text": "hundred and thirty billion dollars, and debt of around forty-seven billion."
  },
  {
   "from": 7021,
   "dur": 88,
   "text": "Which brings us to the problem that no one can code their way around."
  },
  {
   "from": 7124,
   "dur": 22,
   "text": "Electricity."
  },
  {
   "from": 7166,
   "dur": 116,
   "text": "In 2024, the world's data centres used around four hundred and fifteen"
  },
  {
   "from": 7282,
   "dur": 128,
   "text": "terawatt-hours of electricity. About one and a half percent of global demand."
  },
  {
   "from": 7418,
   "dur": 120,
   "text": "The International Energy Agency expects that to more than double by 2030."
  },
  {
   "from": 7545,
   "dur": 86,
   "text": "In the United States, data centres are set to account for"
  },
  {
   "from": 7631,
   "dur": 90,
   "text": "nearly half of all growth in electricity demand this decade."
  },
  {
   "from": 7741,
   "dur": 62,
   "text": "First, the power has to be generated."
  },
  {
   "from": 7803,
   "dur": 97,
   "text": "Big Tech is now signing deals to restart nuclear reactors."
  },
  {
   "from": 7908,
   "dur": 91,
   "text": "Microsoft agreed to buy the output of Three Mile Island's"
  },
  {
   "from": 7999,
   "dur": 81,
   "text": "Unit One for twenty years, if it comes back online."
  },
  {
   "from": 8090,
   "dur": 123,
   "text": "Gas turbines are in such demand that GE Vernova's gas backlog and reserved"
  },
  {
   "from": 8213,
   "dur": 111,
   "text": "production slots have reached one hundred and twenty-two gigawatts."
  },
  {
   "from": 8336,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "Then the power has to be delivered. And here, the bottleneck is physical."
  },
  {
   "from": 8450,
   "dur": 94,
   "text": "Berkeley Lab found that the typical American power project"
  },
  {
   "from": 8544,
   "dur": 100,
   "text": "built in 2025 waited around five years to connect to the grid."
  },
  {
   "from": 8654,
   "dur": 62,
   "text": "And every connection needs transformers."
  },
  {
   "from": 8716,
   "dur": 111,
   "text": "A large power transformer can weigh hundreds of tonnes, and the wait for"
  },
  {
   "from": 8827,
   "dur": 106,
   "text": "one is commonly two years or more. For the largest units, up to four."
  },
  {
   "from": 8941,
   "dur": 105,
   "text": "Prices have climbed too: up sixty to eighty percent since 2020,"
  },
  {
   "from": 9046,
   "dur": 47,
   "text": "according to Wood Mackenzie."
  },
  {
   "from": 9117,
   "dur": 70,
   "text": "This is where some of the quietest fortunes are being made."
  },
  {
   "from": 9198,
   "dur": 141,
   "text": "GE Vernova's order backlog has reached one hundred and ninety-seven billion dollars."
  },
  {
   "from": 9338,
   "dur": 129,
   "text": "Siemens Energy's stands at a record one hundred and sixty-four billion euros."
  },
  {
   "from": 9475,
   "dur": 103,
   "text": "Quanta Services, which builds power lines and substations,"
  },
  {
   "from": 9578,
   "dur": 103,
   "text": "has a record backlog of nearly sixty-four billion dollars."
  },
  {
   "from": 9681,
   "dur": 99,
   "text": "And cable maker Prysmian posted record earnings in 2025."
  },
  {
   "from": 9790,
   "dur": 45,
   "text": "They do not sell intelligence."
  },
  {
   "from": 9835,
   "dur": 91,
   "text": "They sell the physical capacity that intelligence depends on."
  },
  {
   "from": 9971,
   "dur": 34,
   "text": "So who actually wins?"
  },
  {
   "from": 10020,
   "dur": 80,
   "text": "The chip designers capture the richest margins today,"
  },
  {
   "from": 10100,
   "dur": 88,
   "text": "but they depend on a handful of buyers. Earlier this year,"
  },
  {
   "from": 10188,
   "dur": 109,
   "text": "three direct customers accounted for more than half of Nvidia's revenue."
  },
  {
   "from": 10306,
   "dur": 123,
   "text": "The foundries and toolmakers hold positions that are almost impossible to copy,"
  },
  {
   "from": 10428,
   "dur": 101,
   "text": "but they must keep investing tens of billions just to stay ahead."
  },
  {
   "from": 10538,
   "dur": 66,
   "text": "The cloud giants carry the biggest bill of all,"
  },
  {
   "from": 10605,
   "dur": 100,
   "text": "and investors are watching how much of that spending turns into profit."
  },
  {
   "from": 10714,
   "dur": 68,
   "text": "The grid's equipment makers have something rarer:"
  },
  {
   "from": 10781,
   "dur": 93,
   "text": "order books that stretch for years, from customers who cannot wait."
  },
  {
   "from": 10884,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "And someone has to pay. On America's largest grid, run by PJM,"
  },
  {
   "from": 10988,
   "dur": 138,
   "text": "the price of capacity has jumped more than tenfold in three years. Its independent"
  },
  {
   "from": 11125,
   "dur": 138,
   "text": "market monitor attributes more than twenty-three billion dollars of added capacity"
  },
  {
   "from": 11263,
   "dur": 133,
   "text": "costs to data centre demand. Costs that are passed on to electricity customers."
  },
  {
   "from": 11407,
   "dur": 128,
   "text": "None of this guarantees the future. Backlogs can shrink. Forecasts can be wrong."
  },
  {
   "from": 11535,
   "dur": 91,
   "text": "And capacity built for a boom can sit idle in a downturn."
  },
  {
   "from": 11674,
   "dur": 101,
   "text": "The AI revolution is usually told as a story about software."
  },
  {
   "from": 11786,
   "dur": 68,
   "text": "But follow the money, and it leads somewhere else."
  },
  {
   "from": 11854,
   "dur": 86,
   "text": "To chip plants in Taiwan and machine makers in the Netherlands."
  },
  {
   "from": 11948,
   "dur": 125,
   "text": "To cooling plants and cable mills. To turbines, transformers and power lines."
  },
  {
   "from": 12085,
   "dur": 104,
   "text": "The intelligence may be artificial. The infrastructure is very real."
  },
  {
   "from": 12204,
   "dur": 111,
   "text": "And the companies building it may turn out to be the hidden winners of the AI boom."
  }
 ],
 "showCaptions": false
}